WEBVTT

02:49.337 --> 02:52.915
Good morning and welcome to our special council meeting

02:53.011 --> 02:56.589
on March 10th, 2026. The purpose of this meeting

02:56.637 --> 03:00.151
is to consider a bylaw to appoint the Chief Administrative Officer

03:00.311 --> 03:03.599
of the Region of Waterloo. I will now call on Tim Brubacher,

03:03.615 --> 03:07.462
Regional Clerk, to conduct the roll call. Thank you, Regional Chair Redman.

03:07.542 --> 03:10.829
Present. Councillor Craig. Councillor Erb.

03:11.053 --> 03:14.083
Present. Councillor Foxton. Present. Councillor Gowing.

03:14.355 --> 03:17.850
Present. Councillor Harris. Present. Councillor Huinink. Happy St.

03:17.930 --> 03:21.024
Patrick's Day. Councillor James. Present. Councillor Liggett.

03:22.130 --> 03:24.631
Councillor McCabe. Councillor Nowak.

03:25.721 --> 03:28.109
Councillor Rodrigues. Present. Councillor Salonen.

03:29.425 --> 03:32.235
Councillor Schantz. Present. Councillor Vrbanovic. Here.

03:33.102 --> 03:36.490
And Councillor Wolf. Present. I'd like

03:36.990 --> 03:40.553
to acknowledge that the land on which we gather today is the traditional territory

03:40.585 --> 03:43.603
of the Haudenosaunee, the Anishinaabe, and the Chonnonton peoples.

03:44.358 --> 03:47.312
In doing so, I want to reflect on what it means to be doing important

03:47.812 --> 03:50.154
community work like we are engaging in collectively today,

03:50.781 --> 03:53.671
and also on my own individual relationship to this land.

03:54.699 --> 03:58.732
As a settler, one of the most important aspects of my individual journey towards truth

03:59.232 --> 04:02.877
and reconciliation has been to listen. I am continually grateful

04:02.989 --> 04:06.186
to the community who shares their stories and concerns with me.

04:07.166 --> 04:10.669
As well as Chair of the Region of Waterloo, I know I carry a large

04:10.701 --> 04:14.268
responsibility to ensure that it's not just myself on an individual

04:14.782 --> 04:18.332
level listening and acting, but that as a government we are listening and

04:18.832 --> 04:22.874
creating action in our community. I'm also offering this acknowledgement as

04:22.970 --> 04:26.481
one of the many actions I personally and the Region largely is

04:26.513 --> 04:29.045
taking on our journey towards reconciliation.

04:29.943 --> 04:33.342
We acknowledge the enduring presence of the Indigenous people with whom we share

04:33.726 --> 04:37.541
this land today, their achievements and their contributions to our community.

04:38.615 --> 04:41.469
There are a few days of significance I'd also like to recognize.

04:42.703 --> 04:46.663
On March 8th, we celebrated International Women's Day. This day is

04:46.711 --> 04:49.917
an opportunity to recognize the contributions, resilience and

04:50.417 --> 04:53.171
leadership of women within our organization and beyond.

04:54.261 --> 04:58.829
March 15th is International Day to Combat

04:59.134 --> 05:02.773
Islamophobia, which aims to raise global awareness

05:02.821 --> 05:05.819
of rising hatred and promotes tolerance,

05:06.332 --> 05:11.077
interfaith harmony, while urging action against structural

05:11.557 --> 05:14.138
racism and Islamophobia.

05:16.992 --> 05:20.598
It is also currently Ramadan and Lent. Please feel free to use

05:21.098 --> 05:24.687
the multi-faith space in room 221 that provides space

05:25.187 --> 05:28.043
for prayer, reflection, and access to the wudu room.

05:29.183 --> 05:32.459
Uh, you may ask security staff for access to the space.

05:33.455 --> 05:36.907
Colleagues, are there any declarations of pecuniary interest under

05:37.407 --> 05:38.690
the Municipal Conflict of Interest Act?

05:40.681 --> 05:44.294
Seeing none, before we consider the bylaw to appoint the

05:44.794 --> 05:48.196
Chief Administrative Officer, I wanted to let Darshpreet Bhatti

05:48.469 --> 05:51.649
introduce himself as we welcome him back to the region.

05:52.002 --> 05:55.544
Dharspreet. Thank you, Chair. Good morning, everyone.

05:55.608 --> 05:58.847
My name is Dharspreet Singh Bhatti, for those who have not met yet. Uh,

05:59.360 --> 06:02.501
I just will keep this brief and thank Council for your trust in me.

06:03.207 --> 06:07.086
I recognize the responsibility that comes with this position, and I look forward to

06:07.294 --> 06:10.613
listening, learning, and achieving priorities that matter most

06:11.113 --> 06:12.200
to our community. Thank you.

06:14.989 --> 06:18.099
Thank you. So we will now consider a vote to approve,

06:18.275 --> 06:22.427
uh, the Appointment Bylaw 26-011 as

06:22.523 --> 06:26.483
listed on the agenda. If I could have a mover. Moved by Councillor

06:26.547 --> 06:30.634
Wolf, seconded by Councillor James. We are— we will use

06:31.134 --> 06:34.882
eScribe, and the motion is that bylaw to provide the appointment of

06:35.382 --> 06:40.942
the Chief Administrative Officer and repeal bylaws 20-027,

06:41.375 --> 06:46.392
22-023, and 25-019,

06:46.504 --> 06:49.261
and be read for the first, second, and third time,

06:49.774 --> 06:53.285
finally passed and numbered 26-011,

06:53.798 --> 06:57.504
be signed by the Regional Chair and the Clerk and sealed with the regional

06:58.004 --> 07:00.137
seal. Please cast your ballot.

07:22.919 --> 07:26.606
Colleagues, that is carried. And before we move to adjournment, I just really want

07:27.106 --> 07:30.469
to comment on the, um, the bench strength that we

07:30.969 --> 07:34.621
have at the Region of Waterloo, the amazing people who have stepped up and

07:34.637 --> 07:38.869
taken on additional tasks and portfolios, and thank

07:39.369 --> 07:43.004
them for their vision, the decisions that were made, and the fact that it

07:43.053 --> 07:46.259
wasn't ever, in my view, a caretaker

07:46.759 --> 07:50.202
period of time at the Region of Waterloo. We moved very important

07:50.702 --> 07:53.521
strategic things forward on behalf of our community,

07:54.099 --> 07:58.418
and I want to thank all of them for the additional responsibility

07:58.434 --> 08:01.389
they shouldered and the fine way that they served this community.

08:02.802 --> 08:06.238
I now would entertain a motion to adjourn. Moved by

08:06.738 --> 08:10.172
Councillor Harris, seconded by Councillor Vrbanovic. Please use your eScribe

08:10.236 --> 08:10.653
to vote.

08:26.629 --> 08:29.685
Colleagues, that is carried. I think we will have a

08:30.185 --> 08:32.677
2-minute pause to regroup and then we will start committee day.
